# Kiki-Jiki's token copy is to be sacrificed "at the beginning of the next end step" by the delayed ability's controller,
# Bot1; a player can't sacrifice a permanent they don't control (CR 701.21a). With that ability on the stack in Bot1's end
# step, Bot2 takes the token with Old Man of the Sea (Bot2 has controlled Old Man since their turn began, CR 302.6; the
# ability works at instant speed; the token's power 1 is no more than Old Man's 2). The delayed ability resolves and
# sacrifices nothing: the token stays Bot2's for as long as Old Man stays tapped (CR 611.2b), which Bot2 chooses in their
# untap step (CR 502.3). It is a token, with the haste its copy effect gave it (CR 707.9b), whoever controls it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
